> fit <- cfa.run(dataframe, cfa_structure)
> summary(fit)
>
> What I want to do, for example, is return specific values like the p-value.

If you want the p value for the chi-squared statistic, you can get it from the vector returned by fitMeasures(fit)

If you want the p values for the parameter estimates, you can get them from the "pvalue" column in the output of parameterEstimates(fit)

Terry

