Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/Of502TNcg8k/m/5kl5p8SgQioJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It would help to see your model syntax. Is this a CFA or a MIMIC model?  If the latent variables are predicted by other variables, then you are comparing latent intercepts, but if the latent variables are exogenous, then you are comparing latent means (because in an intercept-only model, the intercept is the grand mean).

To be clear, your use of group.equal = c("loadings","intercepts") only constrains the indicator intercepts to equality across groups (countries, in your data).  That does not constrain any latent parameters, nor does it constrain indicator intercepts to zero.  Unless you have constrained indicator intercepts to zero in the model syntax, then they should be freely estimated by default (even if they are constrained to equality across groups).

Please provide your model syntax so that we can see what exactly it is that you want to compare.

Terry

