On 03/20/2015 03:40 PM, Bill Shipley wrote:
> Hello.  I was surprised to read, in Beaujean’s book « Latent variable
> modeling using R », that there is a special operator for specifying
> formative latents : « <~ ».  This doesn’t appear in any other
> documentation that I have found for lavaan

True. The lavaan documentation needs a serious update.

The "<~" operator is just syntax candy. It creates a latent variable
(with no indicators), and sets the (possibly residual) variance of this
latent variable to zero.

So this syntax:

f <~ 1*x1 + x2 + x3

is equivalent to

f =~ 0
f ~~ 0*f
f ~ 1*x1 + x2 + x3

Yves.

